From 1c455d475ca3217e002a74eb08c34d6aad59fcfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:24:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: tb522fu: isolate touch for bounded wake
 diagnosis

Disable only the touchscreen node for one recorded display wake test.
This isolates Linux touch suspend, firmware reload and IRQ activity from
the shared display/TDDI path. Keep the SPI controller, physical keyboard,
panel supplies, commands, PHYs and clock mapping unchanged.

This is a diagnostic discriminator, not a touch or display fix. Require
initial physical pixels, absence of the touch driver/device/input nodes,
one recorded DPMS cycle and exact restoration. Keep the accepted installed
image. Remove this patch before any production acceptance.

Validation: complete sorted DT comparison changes only touchscreen status;
DT compilation and strict checkpatch pass. Runtime guards reject unexpected
module, device, input, enabled-node and missing-node states.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
index c4ac03c32119..522abd9ed6d7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-lenovo-y900-acm.dts
@@ -465,7 +465,8 @@ touchscreen@0 {
 		novatek,pen-support;
 		novatek,spi-rd-fast-addr = <0>;
 
-		status = "okay";
+		/* Diagnostic only: isolate Linux touch activity from display wake. */
+		status = "disabled";
 	};
 };
 
